# A copy of the sha256 Buildroot ships for u-boot 2026.01, so that the check
# outlives Buildroot's default moving on.
#
# We pin the version rather than follow BR2_TARGET_UBOOT_LATEST_VERSION, so
# that bumping Buildroot cannot move u-boot out from under the two patches next
# to this file. Today the two agree and boot/uboot/uboot.hash covers us. The day
# they diverge, that file lists some other version, no line matches our tarball
# -- and uboot.mk has already added it to BR_NO_CHECK_HASH_FOR precisely
# because the version is pinned, so support/download/check-hash treats the
# missing hash as intentional and lets the download through unverified.
#
# The hash only has to be absent to stop protecting us, which is the kind of
# thing that is worth one duplicated line.
#
# A BR2_GLOBAL_PATCH_DIR entry doubles as a hash-override directory -- Buildroot
# looks for <entry>/<package>/<package>.hash in each of them -- which is why
# this lives in a patch directory. apply-patches only globs *.patch, so it is
# ignored there.
sha256  b60d5865cefdbc75da8da4156c56c458e00de75a49b80c1a2e58a96e30ad0d54  u-boot-2026.01.tar.bz2
